(5050026, 734504, 96924, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jac:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice bullion. Good work on the modeling.<br/>Poor choice of background colour though.<br/>With that lens you could have achieved a better image i''m sure. Can''t really tell where the focus point is. I would have chosen a bigger aperture and focused on the coins. This would have made the bullion blurry and given this shot an overall more interesting feel. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments. The quality of the photo suffered when I converted in PS to a smaller size file. I was in a rush and did it on my laptop last minute before posting it. I noticed it as soon as I received the comment from smudgeSMJ. Others also commented on the same issue and I am very unhappy with myself.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment on the composition and background. I agree in hindsight.</td>', 'Originally posted by Jac: Nice bullion. Good work on the modeling.Poor choice of background colour though.With that lens you could have achieved a better image i''m sure. Can''t really tell where the focus point is. I would have chosen a bigger aperture and focused on the coins. This would have made the bullion blurry and given this shot an overall more interesting feel.   Thanks for the comments. The quality of the photo suffered when I converted in PS to a smaller size file. I was in a rush and did it on my laptop last minute before posting it. I noticed it as soon as I received the comment from smudgeSMJ. Others also commented on the same issue and I am very unhappy with myself. Thanks for the comment on the composition and background. I agree in hindsight.', '2008-11-07 02:04:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5050359, 733026, 99924, '<td valign="top">Nice job in your first challenge.  I like the concept of the poker chip.  Also the way the image is focused in the center and gradually fades out of focus adds a very nice touch.<br/></td>', 'Nice job in your first challenge.  I like the concept of the poker chip.  Also the way the image is focused in the center and gradually fades out of focus adds a very nice touch.', '2008-11-07 10:17:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5050415, 734391, 97893, '<td valign="top">I think shot has been grossly underrated! (Blame it on market downturn :-))<br/> <br/>It is a very nicely thought out and composed shot!</td>', 'I think shot has been grossly underrated! (Blame it on market downturn :-)) It is a very nicely thought out and composed shot!', '2008-11-07 10:58:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5050444, 734474, 83080, '<td valign="top">Wow, I would think about putting this up as a stock photo.  I can imagine journalists using this very effectively as it''s a quite provocative illustration for both sides of the <i>In God We Trust</i> / <i>One Nation Under God</i> legal challenges that Michael Newdow will probably continue to make headlines with.</td>', 'Wow, I would think about putting this up as a stock photo.  I can imagine journalists using this very effectively as it''s a quite provocative illustration for both sides of the In God We Trust / One Nation Under God legal challenges that Michael Newdow will probably continue to make headlines with.', '2008-11-07 11:19:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5050475, 734391, 30982, '<td valign="top">LOL!  I almost submitted something very similar to this!  Instead, I bombed in motion blur...  Yours, is of course, much better edited than mine.  And yeah, I figure the US-centric crowd might not pick up on the money aspect of this, nor on the change in the exchange rate (which is good for me, by the way, since I still get paid in US dollars.)</td>', 'LOL!  I almost submitted something very similar to this!  Instead, I bombed in motion blur...  Yours, is of course, much better edited than mine.  And yeah, I figure the US-centric crowd might not pick up on the money aspect of this, nor on the change in the exchange rate (which is good for me, by the way, since I still get paid in US dollars.)', '2008-11-07 11:36:20.000000', NULL, 0),
