(5053877, 734490, 59029, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by purifier:</b></div><hr/><i> This injection doesn''t look so scary like the other one in the contest, and I love this photo </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL! As the person responsible for the other injection shot - which did finish 12th so not too far behind you :-), a tip of the hat to you and congrats on your red!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Originally posted by purifier: This injection doesn''t look so scary like the other one in the contest, and I love this photo   LOL! As the person responsible for the other injection shot - which did finish 12th so not too far behind you :-), a tip of the hat to you and congrats on your red! Susan', '2008-11-09 16:06:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5054531, 734597, 32108, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your top 10 finish - very well executed.</td>', 'Congrats on your top 10 finish - very well executed.', '2008-11-10 04:32:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5054652, 733467, 67258, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club. <br/> <br/>I am sure that this photo ended up scoring far worse than you had expected.  I am quite sure that the end score was as a result of what many viewers clearly perceived as, at best, a tenuous link to the challenge theme.  Had you entered the same photo in to the monthly Free Study I suspect you would have finished a full point and more ahead.<br/> <br/>Technically the photo is competent, although there are things that could be worked on to bring it up another notch.  Focus is sharp on the centre and near petals, falling off with distance.  Exposure is on the dark side - if you were going for a low-key look, you achieved your aim, if not, you may want to try exposing more to the right of your histogram. The black background provides a sombre and somewhat harsh foil to the rose, although it does allow the red to be seen to good effect.  My main problem with the photo is with the composition - and this is just my personal, subjective view - which feels to me somewhat awkward.  The stem is just visible, and I actually find myself trying to follow it out of the photo, there either isn''t enough of it therem, or there is too much.  If you are to include part of the stem, I feel that a more diagonal composition would be worth considering.<br/> <br/>All in all, a competently taken photograph that missed the mark in terms of the challenge. I look forward to seeing more of your flower photographs as you develop further.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Sara.</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club.  I am sure that this photo ended up scoring far worse than you had expected.  I am quite sure that the end score was as a result of what many viewers clearly perceived as, at best, a tenuous link to the challenge theme.  Had you entered the same photo in to the monthly Free Study I suspect you would have finished a full point and more ahead. Technically the photo is competent, although there are things that could be worked on to bring it up another notch.  Focus is sharp on the centre and near petals, falling off with distance.  Exposure is on the dark side - if you were going for a low-key look, you achieved your aim, if not, you may want to try exposing more to the right of your histogram. The black background provides a sombre and somewhat harsh foil to the rose, although it does allow the red to be seen to good effect.  My main problem with the photo is with the composition - and this is just my personal, subjective view - which feels to me somewhat awkward.  The stem is just visible, and I actually find myself trying to follow it out of the photo, there either isn''t enough of it therem, or there is too much.  If you are to include part of the stem, I feel that a more diagonal composition would be worth considering. All in all, a competently taken photograph that missed the mark in terms of the challenge. I look forward to seeing more of your flower photographs as you develop further. Regards,Sara.', '2008-11-10 08:12:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5057799, 734481, 7473, '<td valign="top">Irene,<br/>   First, let me say that this entry is as beautiful as all of the rest of your entries.  You ability and creativity inspire me evertime i see you pic on the front page to improve my photography skills (not my post processing skills)  Thank you.<br/> <br/>   Second, let me thank you for always having a  a useful comment to make on many of my images.  Thank you again.<br/> <br/>Ben</td>', 'Irene,   First, let me say that this entry is as beautiful as all of the rest of your entries.  You ability and creativity inspire me evertime i see you pic on the front page to improve my photography skills (not my post processing skills)  Thank you.    Second, let me thank you for always having a  a useful comment to make on many of my images.  Thank you again. Ben', '2008-11-11 18:10:48.000000', NULL, 0),
